-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/ffa206e0-d1cd-402c-910a-67a5e394f229
-- title:
--   Verified downset enumeration with an internally constructed power table
-- statement:
--   Let $L,c,z,f\in\mathbb N$, with $c\le L$, and put $C=\sum_{j=0}^c\binom Lj$. Let machine limits satisfy $S\le W$, $f+L+1\le S$, $2^{L+1}\le W$, $z+C\le f$, and $d+L+2\le D$. Suppose $P$ contains the setup body, power-table constructor, downset loop, and recursive layer enumerator. From any integer memory $\mu$, execution on $(L,c,z,f)$ returns $C$ and establishes
--
--   $$
--   \mu'[z:z+C]=\operatorname{enumerateDownset}(L,c),\qquad
--   \mu'(f+i)=2^i\quad(i\le L).
--   $$
--
--   The list contains all subset masks of $[L]$ of size at most $c$ in the prescribed layer order. Time is at most $(c+1)(150((4L+1)C+1)+70)+17L+105$. Every address below $f$ outside the output segment is preserved.
--
--   This removes the need for a caller-supplied power table.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightDownsetEnumerationSetup.lean#L23-L63

